.TH ZEX-INSTALL 1 "2026-07-19" "zex 5.0.0" "Zainium OS"
.SH NAME
zex-install \- install packages on Zainium OS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B elevate zex install
.RI [ \-\-dry\-resolve ]
.RI [ \-\-cache\-only ]
.RI [ \-\-lock\-out\ <path> ]
.IR <package> ...
.br
.B elevate zex install \-\-from\-lock
.I <path>
.br
.B elevate zex install \-\-verify\-lock
.I <path>
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zex install
resolves, downloads, verifies, and installs one or more packages onto
.BR "Zainium OS" .
.PP
Dependencies are resolved by a breadth-first search over each package's
declared
.I depends
tokens
.RI ( "not" " PubGrub \(en that crate exists in the source tree but is not"
wired into the live install path). For every dependency, resolution
prefers the
.I same mirror
the requested package itself came from before falling back to a different
tier, and warns visibly when a fallback happens. Real version constraints
embedded in dependency tokens (e.g.
.IR libfoo>=2.0 )
are checked against the resolved candidate's actual version, and
declared package conflicts are checked bidirectionally against everything
already installed. The full plan (every package, every constraint, every
conflict) is computed
.B before
any download begins; if anything is unsatisfiable the operation is
aborted before any change is made to the system.
.PP
Each package is downloaded from the highest-priority tier that provides
it (T1\(enT4) and cryptographically verified against that tier's real
signature scheme (Ed25519+Blake3 for Tier 1; RSA for Tiers 2\(en4 \(em
see
.BR zex.toml (5)
for
.IR signature_verification_mode ),
then extracted atomically into
.IR /overlayer/zexlib/union/ .
.PP
An installed-file receipt is written to
.I /overlayer/zexlib/registry/installed/<name>.toml
and a transaction snapshot is created in
.I /overlayer/zexlib/transactions/
to enable rollback.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-resolve
Resolve dependencies and display the install plan without downloading or
installing anything.
.TP
.B \-\-cache\-only
Install from local cache only; abort if any package is not cached. Useful
for offline environments.
.TP
.BI \-\-lock\-out\  path
After a successful single-package install, write a lockfile to
.I path
recording the exact resolved root and dependency graph (versions, source
mirrors, URLs, hashes). Only supported for single-package installs.
.TP
.BI \-\-from\-lock\  path
Install exactly what the lockfile at
.I path
pins, bypassing live dependency resolution entirely \(em the result is
identical to when the lockfile was generated even if upstream indices
have since changed. Goes through the same download/verify/install
pipeline as a normal install, so signature and hash verification are not
skipped, only name resolution is. Cannot be combined with naming packages
on the command line.
.TP
.BI \-\-verify\-lock\  path
Compare the lockfile at
.I path
against the real, currently-installed registry state and report any
version or hash drift, without installing anything. Exits non-zero if
drift is found. Cannot be combined with naming packages on the command line.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All packages installed successfully (or, for
.BR \-\-verify\-lock ,
no drift found).
.TP
.B 1
Dependency conflict, version-constraint violation, download failure,
signature/hash verification failure, insufficient privileges, or (for
.BR \-\-verify\-lock )
drift found.
.SH EXAMPLES
Install a single package:
.PP
.nf
    elevate zex install ripgrep
.fi
.PP
Install multiple packages:
.PP
.nf
    elevate zex install vim htop curl fd-find
.fi
.PP
Preview what would be installed:
.PP
.nf
    elevate zex install neovim --dry-resolve
.fi
.PP
Pin an install for later exact reproduction:
.PP
.nf
    elevate zex install musl --lock-out musl.lock.toml
    # ... later, on any host ...
    elevate zex install --from-lock musl.lock.toml
.fi
.PP
Check whether a previously-locked install has drifted:
.PP
.nf
    elevate zex install --verify-lock musl.lock.toml
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /overlayer/zexlib/registry/installed/<name>.toml
Package receipt written after successful installation \(em the
authoritative record of what is installed.
.TP
.I /overlayer/zexlib/registry/packages.toml
Derived summary index, kept in sync automatically; regenerable from
scratch with
.BR "zex doctor --fix" .
.TP
.I /overlayer/zexlib/transactions/tx-<timestamp>/
Snapshot directory for rollback.
.TP
.I /overlayer/zexlib/tmp/
Temporary extraction area, cleaned after install.
.TP
.I /var/lib/zex/history.json
Every install is recorded here; query with
.BR zex-history (1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zex (1),
.BR zex-remove (1),
.BR zex-rollback (1),
.BR zex-inspect (1),
.BR zex-history (1)
